        "# Llm Fine Tuning - mod-10\n\n",
        "**Course:** llm-fine-tuning\n\n",
        "Run the code cells below to practice.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt: \"Explain quantum entanglement in simple terms\"\n\nOutput A (by Model 1):\n\"Quantum entanglement occurs when particles become connected such that \nmeasuring one instantly affects the other, regardless of distance. \nEinstein called this 'spooky action at a distance.'\"\n\nOutput B (by Model 2):\n\"Entanglement is when particles are related. If you measure one, the other \none is affected. This happens very fast. It's weird but true.\"\n\nHuman Annotation: Output A is better (clearer explanation, more complete)\nLabel: A > B"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "# Reward model training concept\n\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForSequenceClassification, AutoTokenizer\n\n# Load a model for classification\nreward_model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\n    \"meta-llama/Llama-2-7b\",\n    num_labels=1  # Output single score, not classification\n)\n\n# Remove the language modeling head, use classification head instead\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"meta-llama/Llama-2-7b\")\n\n# Training setup\noptimizer = torch.optim.Adam(reward_model.parameters(), lr=1e-5)\ncriterion = torch.nn.MSELoss()  # Or ranking loss\n\n# During training, for each preference pair:\n# - Forward pass: compute scores for preferred output\n# - Forward pass: compute scores for non-preferred output\n# - Loss: prefer_score > non_prefer_score (margin loss typical)\n\ndef ranking_loss(preferred_score, non_preferred_score, margin=0.5):\n    \"\"\"Margin ranking loss: penalize if preferred_score isn't sufficiently higher\"\"\"\n    return torch.nn.functional.margin_ranking_loss(\n        torch.ones_like(preferred_score),\n        preferred_score,\n        non_preferred_score,\n        margin=margin\n    )"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "1. Initialize: LLM, Reward Model, Reference Model (frozen copy of initial LLM)\n\n2. For each training iteration:\n   a) Generate outputs using current LLM\n   b) Score outputs using Reward Model\n   c) Compute reward advantage:\n      advantage = reward - (reference_model_logprob - current_model_logprob)\n      (penalizes diverging too much from initial model)\n   d) Update LLM using PPO to maximize advantage\n   e) Periodically re-collect new batches"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "# Pseudocode of PPO update step\n\ndef ppo_update(model, ref_model, reward_model, prompt_batch, learning_rate=1e-5):\n    \"\"\"One PPO update step\"\"\"\n    \n    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=learning_rate)\n    \n    for prompt in prompt_batch:\n        # Generate output\n        with torch.no_grad():\n            output = model.generate(prompt, max_length=100)\n            reward = reward_model(prompt, output)\n            ref_logprob = ref_model(prompt, output).log_probs\n            \n        # Current model's log probability\n        model_logprob = model(prompt, output).log_probs\n        \n        # Ratio for PPO\n        ratio = torch.exp(model_logprob - ref_logprob)\n        \n        # PPO loss (simplified; actual implementation is more complex)\n        advantage = reward - (ref_logprob - model_logprob) * 0.1  # KL coefficient\n        \n        # Clip ratio to prevent large policy changes (PPO's key feature)\n        clipped_ratio = torch.clamp(ratio, 0.9, 1.1)\n        loss = -torch.min(ratio * advantage, clipped_ratio * advantage).mean()\n        \n        # Update\n        optimizer.zero_grad()\n        loss.backward()\n        optimizer.step()\n    \n    return loss.item()"
        ]
      ]
    },
